# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# This tree came from a Windows-first checkout and every file in the working copy still
# has CRLF endings, while the git blobs hold LF. That produced a permanent phantom diff —
# `git diff --stat` reported 63 files and 9416 insertions / 9416 deletions with ZERO
# content difference, which made "is this tree dirty?" unanswerable at a glance.
#
# `text=auto` stores LF in the repository and checks out the platform's native ending, so
# the diff reflects real changes only.
* text=auto

# Explicitly binary, so git never tries to normalise or diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.deb binary
*.zip binary

# Shell scripts and Rust stay LF even on Windows: a CRLF shebang line is not executable.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
